with every version; AGENTS.md: the replica is its own product.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] share-takes-gallery-videos
Photos and videos shared from the Gallery, one or several, mixed or not, MUST save
as cards. The share target MUST take files as big as an upload from inside the app
(5 GB), not mymind's 25 MB, since a phone's videos are mostly bigger than that.
A saved video's speech is transcribed on the server and shown in the reader as its
Transcript (`card-reader-shows-the-whole-card`).
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026: "You should be able to save videos and images
directly into the app ... share from my Gallery ... And when videos are shared, we
transcribe them." The same day he moved transcription from xAI to OpenAI's latest
model ("Let's use OpenAI's API for this"), and raised the limit from 500 MB to
5 GB ("Let's raise it to 5GB, actually. That makes it very useful."). The reader
section is Claude's choice.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] share-reads-gallery-in-place
A shared photo or video that the Gallery keeps on the phone (its own MediaStore
entry, or the one a Google Photos link wraps) MUST upload from that file, without a
copy on the phone, when Inventory holds full photo and video access. Inventory MUST ask
for that access at most once, before saving a share that holds such an item, and
MUST NOT ask for anything else. Without full access (refused, or only some photos
allowed) and for every other shared file, the share MUST still save from a copy.
Inventory MUST NOT read a Gallery entry, in place or to copy it, unless the share
carried a read grant (Android grants only what the sender could read), and MUST
unwrap a Google Photos link only when that authority belongs to the preinstalled
Google Photos, so another app cannot use Inventory's access to read the Gallery.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026, chose "Read from the Gallery" over copying, because a
5 GB video needed 5 GB free on the phone.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] share-sheet-shows-thymind-tags
When one thing is shared, the sheet MUST show the tags Inventory gave it as soon
as they reach the phone, before the tags the user added, each marked with the
spark and taken off by a tap. Until they arrive it MUST show a Finding tags chip
in their place. A tag taken off MUST come off the card when the sheet goes, and
choosing that tag again in the field MUST put it back. The phone MUST look for
them at least every second while it waits, and the server MUST start tagging a
link as soon as its words are read, not after its pictures and screenshot.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026: "the moment I share them and I see the little
tag screen where I can add my own tags, I should already see tags that Jev
generated" (Jev was the tag judge then; OpenAI's Decisions API took its place
the same day). This replaces the share prototype's choice to leave Inventory's tags
off the sheet.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] share-sheet-says-when-merged
When Inventory finds that one thing just shared is the same thing as a card saved
before (the same page, post, video, picture, file or note, even at another
address), the server MUST fold the new save into the earlier card: its own
tags, note and spaces move over, the earlier card comes to the top, and the new
copy goes to the trash where it can be restored. The share sheet MUST then show
the earlier card, titled Merged with an earlier save, and spaces, tags and a note
added on the sheet MUST reach the earlier card. Only a near-certain match is
merged, and only for something saved in the last half hour.
Source: Tavi's pick on 5 November 2026, "Merge into the earlier card", over
keeping both or a review list.
